BT 1 0 0 1 0 17 Tm /F1 9 Tf 13 TL (Use the six implementations from Problems 1-6 without their step-by-step trace output. Count comparisons on the required) Tj T* (input patterns, then benchmark each algorithm on identical random data for each size.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 52.8 371.48 cm
%PreformattedPara
.090196 .129412 .168627 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 3 284 Tm /F3 7.2 Tf 9.1 TL (ALGORITHM COMPARE-SIX-SORTS) Tj T* (    A <- [34, 7, 23, 32, 5, 62, 14, 19]) Tj T* (    SORTS <- [Bubble, Insertion, Selection, Quick, Merge, Heap]) Tj T* (    INPUTS <- [A, sorted copy of A, reverse-sorted copy of A]) Tj T*  T* (    for each input in INPUTS do) Tj T* (        for each sort in SORTS do) Tj T* (            values <- copy\(input\)) Tj T* (            comparisons <- 0) Tj T* (            run sort\(values\) with step-by-step tracing disabled) Tj T* (            print sort name, input name, comparisons) Tj T* (            print first min\(10, length\(values\)\) values using printArray) Tj T* (        end for) Tj T* (    end for) Tj T*  T* (    for n in [1000, 5000, 10000] do) Tj T* (        randomData <- n random integers in [1, 100000]) Tj T* (        for each sort in SORTS do) Tj T* (            values <- copy\(randomData\)       // same data for every sort) Tj T* (            start <- high-resolution clock) Tj T* (            run sort\(values\) with tracing disabled) Tj T* (            elapsed <- stop clock - start) Tj T* (            print n, sort name, elapsed time) Tj T* (            print first min\(10, n\) values using printArray) Tj T* (        end for) Tj T* (    end for) Tj T*  T* (    compare measured counts and times with expected growth rates) Tj T* (    identify algorithms with quadratic and n log n growth) Tj T* (    explain whether measurements agree with theory) Tj T* (    recommend a sort for large random and nearly sorted inputs) Tj T* (END ALGORITHM) Tj T* ET
Q
q
